id: pm-pr1569-review
title: "PR1569: prove invalid rollback refuses without mutating a matching item"
description: "CodeRabbit review comment4365313003 on PR1569 identifies a test-coverage gap rather than a runtime defect. The current validator is early, but the fixture has no matching row and only checks rejection. Strengthen the observable acceptance without adding a production test seam. Add concise safety-contract documentation to touched private writers and retain the user-authorized grouped SDK/security scope."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: changelog-exclude,review,tests
created_at: "2026-10-24T00:34:12.671Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T00:37:00.704Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T00:37:00.088Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-24T00:37:00.088Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: Create a matching item for each invalid rollback input; supply valid forward update and close options; verify full item equality and exact history bytes after each rejection; keep canonical source and hosted checks green
parent: pm-gh1564
risk: low
confidence: 95
resolution: Invalid direct rollback cases now create a matching item and supply valid forward update and close inputs; after each rejection they compare the full item and exact immutable history bytes. Touched private mutation and recovery writers have concise safety-contract docs. Existing security triage ownership prose is represented by related edges.
expected_result: A future validation-order regression cannot mutate a matching item or history while still passing the invalid-input test.
actual_result: "The focused and linked20-test suites pass with the stronger state/history controls; canonical docstring validation passes. First-head hosted coverage and all native/packed/security checks passed; the sole static failure was the now-corrected three-edge graph assertion. The unchanged graph, record-integrity and bounded mutation gates pass."
